{"name":"Aviator","hex":"#7d6049","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aviator","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An aircraft pilot, especially a military pilot. The use of the word may imply claims of superior airmanship, as in navy aviator vs. air force pilot.","An experimenter in aviation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aviator"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aviator (Ukrainian band)","blocks":[{"text":"AVIATOR is a Ukrainian band, which was formed in 2005 in Kyiv, Ukraine. From the beginning, the group occupied a niche of the romantic character of pop-music, and it still remains a leader of the field. The release of the debut album \"V efire\" made a splash on the national show-business market: for the first week, the band sold over 50,000 of copies, and, in total, the album has been sold in over 200,000 copies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/%D0%90%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80_-_%D1%84%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%BE.JPG/330px-%D0%90%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80_-_%D1%84%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%BE.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aviator_(Ukrainian_band)"},{"title":"Aircraft pilot","blocks":[{"text":"An aircraft pilot is an individual who controls an aircraft's flight by operating its directional controls. Other aircrew members, such as navigators and flight engineers, are also considered aviators because they assist in operating the aircraft’s navigation and engine systems. Aircrew members like drone operators, flight attendants, mechanics, and ground crew are not classified as aviators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Lt_Mike_Hunter_1.jpg/330px-Lt_Mike_Hunter_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aircraft_pilot"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Transaero_777